{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>My spirit shall not contend with man forever, for that he is also flesh.</b> It is not fitting that he should ever have contention before Me and opening of the mouth to argue and say: even though man deserves severe punishment for his rebellion, because he possesses the image and likeness, nevertheless he also deserves compassion, for it is also his flesh that leads him to sin — not the image and likeness alone.</i>" "<b>And his days shall be.</b> He shall have time for repentance." "<b>A hundred and twenty years.</b> For during that time Noah was building the ark and reproving them and warning them, as per the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 108b)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The syntax of the Hebrew embeds the imagined argument within Elohim's reasoning; the translation preserves Sforno's structure of a hypothetical plea for compassion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:16.188455548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}